1
00:00:01,209 --> 00:00:04,004
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

2
00:00:04,087 --> 00:00:08,425
[MAMANG SASTRE PLAYING]

3
00:00:09,426 --> 00:00:10,927
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

4
00:00:11,010 --> 00:00:12,846
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

5
00:00:16,850 --> 00:00:20,478
I called you because of this.

6
00:00:20,562 --> 00:00:22,063
- Paldo: Zombie run.
- Velma: Zombie run.

7
00:00:22,147 --> 00:00:23,982
Laboratory head:
This is a new side effect.

8
00:00:24,065 --> 00:00:26,735
These do not belong
to the expected responses.

9
00:00:26,818 --> 00:00:30,238
A certain Belladonna texted Atoy.

10
00:00:30,321 --> 00:00:32,073
So, I'll keep an eye on my husband.

11
00:00:32,157 --> 00:00:33,116
Emerson: That face.

12
00:00:33,199 --> 00:00:35,243
Remember, that's the two-timing Elvis.

13
00:00:35,326 --> 00:00:36,703
That's who we're looking for.

14
00:00:36,786 --> 00:00:38,580
It’s Elvis? There, look.

15
00:00:38,663 --> 00:00:39,539
That's so unfair, you know.

16
00:00:39,622 --> 00:00:41,833
The deal was we'd both wear costumes.

17
00:00:41,916 --> 00:00:42,667
It's a prank!

18
00:00:42,751 --> 00:00:44,294
I need to hide…

19
00:00:44,377 --> 00:00:45,920
… your face because he might see you--

20
00:00:46,004 --> 00:00:47,297
- Oop, sorry.
- Miss!

21
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:49,007
Go!

22
00:00:49,090 --> 00:00:50,300
[whooping]

23
00:00:50,383 --> 00:00:52,343
Goon: Sir, where do we
dispose of the body?

24
00:00:52,427 --> 00:00:53,303
It's up to you.

25
00:00:53,386 --> 00:00:54,262
Come on, come on.

26
00:00:54,345 --> 00:00:55,930
Gavin! That's Gavin.

27
00:00:56,014 --> 00:00:57,432
Jesabel: There's the zombie run, look.

28
00:00:57,515 --> 00:00:59,309
It's close to Master Cutter's event.

29
00:00:59,392 --> 00:01:00,477
I've noticed,

30
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:02,187
it's been following us for a while.

31
00:01:02,270 --> 00:01:03,438
Get out of there!

32
00:01:03,521 --> 00:01:04,564
I told you, you can't--

33
00:01:05,190 --> 00:01:06,107
SOS.

34
00:01:06,191 --> 00:01:07,108
Atoy!

35
00:01:07,192 --> 00:01:08,568
On my way. I'm on my way.

36
00:01:09,235 --> 00:01:10,236
Gavin!

37
00:01:10,320 --> 00:01:11,362
[growls]

38
00:01:11,446 --> 00:01:12,989
[zipping & rustling]

39
00:01:13,073 --> 00:01:13,907
[pants]

40
00:01:14,574 --> 00:01:15,825
Belladonna: You need me, right?

41
00:01:15,909 --> 00:01:16,743
Who are you?

42
00:01:16,826 --> 00:01:17,911
I'm the Belladonna.

43
00:01:17,994 --> 00:01:19,788
[grunting & groaning]

44
00:01:19,871 --> 00:01:20,455
Take Uno with you,

45
00:01:20,538 --> 00:01:21,915
go to the auto repair shop.

46
00:01:21,998 --> 00:01:22,540
- Belladonna: Okay, Sir.
- Okay, okay?

47
00:01:22,624 --> 00:01:23,625
Do you know, the one
I was chasing?

48
00:01:23,708 --> 00:01:24,751
That's someone I chat with.

49
00:01:24,834 --> 00:01:27,295
I really wanted to meet her IRL.

50
00:01:27,378 --> 00:01:30,089
[groaning, lively chatter]
[high-pitched ping sound]

51
00:01:30,715 --> 00:01:32,175
Bro, are you okay?

52
00:01:38,681 --> 00:01:40,475
Help! Help!

53
00:01:40,558 --> 00:01:41,768
Oh no! He bit me! Hey!

54
00:01:41,851 --> 00:01:43,102
(Fix this)

55
00:01:43,186 --> 00:01:44,521
Be alert, okay.

56
00:01:45,188 --> 00:01:47,190
You might see Atoy!

57
00:01:47,273 --> 00:01:48,733
How will we recognize Atoy?

58
00:01:48,817 --> 00:01:50,527
Maybe he's wearing a zombie costume too.

59
00:01:50,610 --> 00:01:53,113
Help! Help!

60
00:01:53,196 --> 00:01:54,739
There's a zombie!

61
00:01:54,823 --> 00:01:56,491
Huh? Well, of course! It's a zombie run.

62
00:01:56,574 --> 00:01:57,784
What are you saying?

63
00:01:57,867 --> 00:01:58,993
A real zombie, Sir!

64
00:01:59,077 --> 00:02:00,620
It bites, Sir!

65
00:02:00,703 --> 00:02:01,913
Help! Help!

66
00:02:02,455 --> 00:02:03,039
[Elias gasps]

67
00:02:03,123 --> 00:02:05,917
A zombie bit me!

68
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,128
My God! I feel like I'm going to faint.

69
00:02:08,211 --> 00:02:08,878
[breathes heavily]

70
00:02:08,962 --> 00:02:10,171
Oh my, Sir!

71
00:02:10,255 --> 00:02:11,923
Hey! Stop being dramatic.

72
00:02:12,006 --> 00:02:13,383
Pretending to faint.

73
00:02:13,466 --> 00:02:15,093
- No, Sir.
- What are--

74
00:02:15,176 --> 00:02:16,761
We're telling the truth, Sir.

75
00:02:16,845 --> 00:02:17,637
[wailing & screaming]

76
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:19,305
What are these people saying?

77
00:02:19,389 --> 00:02:21,182
[screaming & panicking]

78
00:02:21,891 --> 00:02:24,936
[sneaky music playing]

79
00:02:25,019 --> 00:02:27,564
There's a zombie there!
There's a zombie there!

80
00:02:29,065 --> 00:02:30,984
What zombie are you talking about?

81
00:02:31,067 --> 00:02:31,818
You're so overdramatic.

82
00:02:31,901 --> 00:02:33,111
It's a zombie run!

83
00:02:33,194 --> 00:02:34,362
Huh? What zombie?

84
00:02:34,445 --> 00:02:35,864
Are you guys kidding me?

85
00:02:35,947 --> 00:02:37,532
Here he comes! Here he comes!

86
00:02:37,615 --> 00:02:41,286
[screaming & panicking]

87
00:02:44,164 --> 00:02:44,747
You're so extra,

88
00:02:44,831 --> 00:02:46,207
like you've seen a celebrity.

89
00:02:46,291 --> 00:02:47,292
You're so overdramatic.

90
00:02:47,375 --> 00:02:50,003
It's just me, Emerson, I'm
just in zombie mode.

91
00:02:50,086 --> 00:02:51,004
You guys, really.

92
00:02:51,629 --> 00:02:52,964
- What--what is this nonsense?
- There's--there's a zombie!

93
00:02:53,047 --> 00:02:53,673
There's a zombie!

94
00:02:53,756 --> 00:02:55,508
- Where's the zombie? Where?
- There's a zombie over there! It bites!

95
00:02:55,592 --> 00:02:56,968
Yes, indeed.
There's--there really is a zombie--

96
00:02:57,051 --> 00:02:59,178
[screaming & panicking]

97
00:02:59,262 --> 00:03:00,430
Here it comes!

98
00:03:08,229 --> 00:03:09,230
Hey, hey!

99
00:03:09,689 --> 00:03:10,940
What are you doing?!

100
00:03:11,024 --> 00:03:12,650
[screaming & panicking]

101
00:03:14,611 --> 00:03:15,862
What zombie?!

102
00:03:15,945 --> 00:03:18,448
[screaming & panicking]

103
00:03:18,531 --> 00:03:21,993
[suspenseful music playing]
[squealing & wailing]

104
00:03:24,412 --> 00:03:26,956
Gavin! Help me!

105
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:30,335
[screaming & panicking]

106
00:03:50,021 --> 00:03:51,481
Hey! Come here!

107
00:03:51,564 --> 00:03:52,732
Hey! Come with us, no fuss!

108
00:03:52,815 --> 00:03:53,650
Sir!

109
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:55,109
We're police, police!

110
00:03:55,193 --> 00:03:56,152
Hey, you!

111
00:03:56,236 --> 00:03:58,363
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor… ♪

112
00:04:00,823 --> 00:04:04,035
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

113
00:04:04,118 --> 00:04:06,037
♪ Wait a moment, Mr. Tailor ♪

114
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:07,872
♪ Can you be the one to stitch up ♪

115
00:04:07,956 --> 00:04:09,332
♪ The hole in my polo

116
00:04:09,415 --> 00:04:11,542
that's right under the armpit ♪

117
00:04:11,626 --> 00:04:13,544
♪ In every cut of cloth ♪

118
00:04:13,628 --> 00:04:15,505
♪ There’s a secret behind it ♪

119
00:04:15,588 --> 00:04:17,215
♪ If your measurement is wrong,

120
00:04:17,298 --> 00:04:21,010
the whole fit turns crooked… ♪

121
00:04:22,595 --> 00:04:23,096
[gunshots]

122
00:04:23,179 --> 00:04:24,722
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

123
00:04:24,806 --> 00:04:27,392
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

124
00:04:27,475 --> 00:04:28,184
[music swells]

125
00:04:28,268 --> 00:04:29,894
(Fix this)

126
00:04:31,271 --> 00:04:32,438
[music fades]

127
00:04:34,023 --> 00:04:36,025
Kurt on the phone:
I just talked to Miss Tess.

128
00:04:36,109 --> 00:04:38,444
I sent the photos of her husband earlier,

129
00:04:38,528 --> 00:04:40,947
and as it turns out,

130
00:04:41,030 --> 00:04:43,950
the people with Elvis were his cousins

131
00:04:44,033 --> 00:04:45,910
and nephew!

132
00:04:45,994 --> 00:04:49,163
So, no sighting yet with the mistress.

133
00:04:49,247 --> 00:04:50,206
But, Brother Kurt,

134
00:04:50,832 --> 00:04:52,542
did you see the picture I sent you?

135
00:04:52,625 --> 00:04:53,876
[suspicious music playing]

136
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:55,086
This is the card that fell

137
00:04:55,169 --> 00:04:56,254
from his pocket earlier.

138
00:04:57,255 --> 00:04:58,631
It's a coffee shop card.

139
00:04:59,757 --> 00:05:01,551
Look, he's collecting stickers.

140
00:05:02,385 --> 00:05:05,596
You know, I'm sure this is wherez
he goes on dates.

141
00:05:06,597 --> 00:05:09,851
Why isn't he nervous about his cheating?

142
00:05:09,934 --> 00:05:11,519
Kurt on the phone: When I interviewed
Miss Tess,

143
00:05:12,186 --> 00:05:13,813
she said she's not allowed
to drink coffee.

144
00:05:15,606 --> 00:05:17,358
There! Now we know!

145
00:05:17,442 --> 00:05:19,986
That means the one who goes there
with him isn't Miss Tess,

146
00:05:20,069 --> 00:05:21,487
it's none other than…

147
00:05:22,155 --> 00:05:24,532
Both: Rochelle the side chick!

148
00:05:24,615 --> 00:05:25,491
[rousing music playing]

149
00:05:25,575 --> 00:05:27,493
[screaming & panicking]

150
00:05:27,577 --> 00:05:29,329
Hurry up, Munggo!

151
00:05:29,412 --> 00:05:30,705
Get out of here! Go!

152
00:05:30,788 --> 00:05:32,123
Here comes the zombie!

153
00:05:35,209 --> 00:05:38,671
Paldo, Kap! Kap! Kap!
[screaming & panicking]

154
00:05:38,755 --> 00:05:41,382
He's going to bite Emerson!

155
00:05:41,466 --> 00:05:43,384
The zombie that bites!

156
00:05:43,468 --> 00:05:44,302
Let’s go, let’s go,

157
00:05:44,385 --> 00:05:44,927
Wait. Don't tell me

158
00:05:45,011 --> 00:05:46,304
you believe there's really a zombie?

159
00:05:46,387 --> 00:05:48,931
Ah, me? I--I don't believe it, ah.

160
00:05:49,432 --> 00:05:50,641
Oh, I just need to protect you.

161
00:05:50,725 --> 00:05:51,851
Of course I don't want you to get bitten.

162
00:05:51,934 --> 00:05:52,852
- Huh?
- So, let's go.

163
00:05:52,935 --> 00:05:53,770
Huh?

164
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:55,063
Wait--

165
00:05:55,146 --> 00:05:56,731
[screaming & panicking]

166
00:05:56,814 --> 00:05:58,524
[pleasant music playing]

167
00:06:03,029 --> 00:06:04,197
Elias: Wait!

168
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:05,281
Where are you going?

169
00:06:05,364 --> 00:06:06,532
Hey, stop!

170
00:06:07,366 --> 00:06:08,701
Didn't I say I'm police?

171
00:06:09,702 --> 00:06:10,495
Hey!

172
00:06:10,578 --> 00:06:11,788
[sneaky music playing]

173
00:06:11,871 --> 00:06:13,873
I said stop!

174
00:06:13,956 --> 00:06:15,124
[growling & screaming]

175
00:06:15,208 --> 00:06:16,125
[foreboding music playing]

176
00:06:16,209 --> 00:06:17,001
Shugo: Sir, Sir, Sir!

177
00:06:17,627 --> 00:06:18,961
Ahh, let go of me!

178
00:06:19,045 --> 00:06:20,505
Let go of me! Let go of me!

179
00:06:20,588 --> 00:06:21,464
Hey! Let go of him!

180
00:06:21,547 --> 00:06:22,340
Oh--stop that!

181
00:06:22,423 --> 00:06:23,257
Stop it, hey!

182
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:24,425
[gasps]

183
00:06:24,509 --> 00:06:25,510
Hey, help me!

184
00:06:25,593 --> 00:06:26,803
Sir--Sir, you take care of that!

185
00:06:26,886 --> 00:06:29,472
That's assaulting an officer! Aargh!

186
00:06:29,555 --> 00:06:32,100
That's forbidden! Help!

187
00:06:32,183 --> 00:06:34,352
Don't! Not me!

188
00:06:34,435 --> 00:06:36,479
[wailing & growling]

189
00:06:36,562 --> 00:06:37,313
Shugo: Sir, hold on!

190
00:06:37,396 --> 00:06:38,523
Aargh! Help!

191
00:06:38,606 --> 00:06:39,565
Help!

192
00:06:39,649 --> 00:06:44,487
[growling & screaming]

193
00:06:45,404 --> 00:06:46,864
[grunts]

194
00:06:48,032 --> 00:06:51,828
[growling & grunting]

195
00:06:51,911 --> 00:06:52,745
The Baker!

196
00:06:54,831 --> 00:06:56,749
Sir, Sir, are you okay? Sir, Sir.

197
00:06:56,833 --> 00:06:58,626
Baker, Baker!

198
00:06:58,709 --> 00:06:59,961
I'm Atoy.

199
00:07:00,044 --> 00:07:01,963
I'm Atoy, I'm Master Cutter!

200
00:07:02,046 --> 00:07:02,713
[growls]

201
00:07:02,797 --> 00:07:04,423
Your name is Dickson!

202
00:07:04,507 --> 00:07:05,800
We were together in Tuguegarao!

203
00:07:05,883 --> 00:07:06,801
What happened to you?

204
00:07:06,884 --> 00:07:07,718
[growls]

205
00:07:07,802 --> 00:07:08,928
Dickson!

206
00:07:09,011 --> 00:07:10,555
Listen, okay.

207
00:07:10,638 --> 00:07:12,223
What did Obsidian do to you?

208
00:07:12,306 --> 00:07:14,100
What did Obsidian do to you?!

209
00:07:14,183 --> 00:07:14,892
[growls]

210
00:07:14,976 --> 00:07:16,185
Brother Atoy!

211
00:07:16,269 --> 00:07:16,936
Atoy!

212
00:07:17,019 --> 00:07:18,146
[growling]

213
00:07:18,896 --> 00:07:21,232
[grunts]

214
00:07:21,899 --> 00:07:22,692
I got bitten.

215
00:07:22,775 --> 00:07:23,568
Nothing, Sir--Sir--

216
00:07:23,651 --> 00:07:25,236
Sir, Sir. Sir, how many is this?

217
00:07:25,319 --> 00:07:26,362
[playful music playing]

218
00:07:26,863 --> 00:07:27,530
Okay.

219
00:07:27,613 --> 00:07:28,448
[gasping]

220
00:07:29,574 --> 00:07:31,742
[grunts & groans]

221
00:07:31,826 --> 00:07:32,493
[thuds]

222
00:07:32,577 --> 00:07:33,327
[growling]

223
00:07:33,411 --> 00:07:35,788
Dickson, Dickson!

224
00:07:35,872 --> 00:07:36,998
It’s Atoy!

225
00:07:37,665 --> 00:07:40,585
What did they do to you, huh?

226
00:07:40,668 --> 00:07:42,336
Wh--what do you want to say?

227
00:07:42,420 --> 00:07:43,337
Speak!

228
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:45,423
What did they do to you?!

229
00:07:45,506 --> 00:07:46,799
Dickson!

230
00:07:46,883 --> 00:07:47,467
Atoy, be careful!

231
00:07:47,550 --> 00:07:49,218
He might bite you!
He might have rabies!

232
00:07:49,302 --> 00:07:50,511
[gasping]

233
00:07:52,513 --> 00:07:53,514
I’m Atoy!

234
00:07:54,098 --> 00:07:55,308
We know each other!

235
00:07:55,391 --> 00:07:58,478
We were together! Dickson!

236
00:07:58,561 --> 00:07:59,604
[grunting]

237
00:07:59,687 --> 00:08:02,273
Where did Obsidian take you, huh?!

238
00:08:02,356 --> 00:08:03,691
[heavy music playing]

239
00:08:03,774 --> 00:08:04,609
Dickson.

240
00:08:05,318 --> 00:08:06,235
[grunts & groans]

241
00:08:06,611 --> 00:08:07,987
[growls]

242
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:09,155
I'll give this to you, okay.

243
00:08:09,238 --> 00:08:10,364
Shoot him in the head.

244
00:08:10,448 --> 00:08:11,032
Why the head?

245
00:08:11,115 --> 00:08:12,700
Just the foot so he can't run!

246
00:08:12,783 --> 00:08:14,368
Don't you watch zombie movies?

247
00:08:14,452 --> 00:08:15,244
You shoot them in the head,

248
00:08:15,328 --> 00:08:16,704
so they won’t survive.

249
00:08:16,787 --> 00:08:17,788
[sneaky music playing]

250
00:08:17,872 --> 00:08:18,706
Come on.

251
00:08:18,789 --> 00:08:20,666
Let go! Hey!

252
00:08:20,750 --> 00:08:22,001
[growls]

253
00:08:23,294 --> 00:08:24,462
Dickson, don't!

254
00:08:24,545 --> 00:08:26,005
Dickson, you recognize me.

255
00:08:26,088 --> 00:08:27,298
Let go of him!

256
00:08:27,381 --> 00:08:28,216
Let go!

257
00:08:28,299 --> 00:08:30,009
Don't, don't--don't shoot!

258
00:08:30,092 --> 00:08:30,927
Don't, don't, don't, don't!

259
00:08:33,012 --> 00:08:33,971
Don't--don't--

260
00:08:34,055 --> 00:08:35,097
[grunts]
[thumps]

261
00:08:36,599 --> 00:08:39,519
[heavy music playing]

262
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:54,575
The marshals reported that

263
00:08:54,659 --> 00:08:56,577
someone brought a gun
to the run earlier.

264
00:08:57,161 --> 00:08:58,162
A--a gun? W--what?!

265
00:08:58,246 --> 00:09:00,039
Oh--unconfirmed, but um,

266
00:09:00,122 --> 00:09:01,582
there was no follow-up report either.

267
00:09:02,625 --> 00:09:04,293
Um, ah, was anyone hurt?

268
00:09:04,377 --> 00:09:05,044
Did anyone faint?

269
00:09:05,127 --> 00:09:06,587
Uhm, there's no such report,
but some people tripped,

270
00:09:06,671 --> 00:09:09,632
but they still finished the run.

271
00:09:09,715 --> 00:09:11,342
[pensive music playing]

272
00:09:11,425 --> 00:09:12,802
[screaming]
|Where is Atoy, anyway?

273
00:09:12,885 --> 00:09:15,137
Siony: Zombie! Zombie!

274
00:09:15,221 --> 00:09:15,805
Hey, hey, Miss--

275
00:09:15,888 --> 00:09:16,472
Zombie?

276
00:09:16,556 --> 00:09:17,181
Miss Siony, what is it?

277
00:09:17,265 --> 00:09:17,807
Siony!

278
00:09:17,890 --> 00:09:21,811
Zombie! There's a--there's
a biting--zombie!

279
00:09:21,894 --> 00:09:23,604
Calm down!

280
00:09:23,688 --> 00:09:24,272
Calm down!

281
00:09:24,355 --> 00:09:26,482
What--what kind of gossip
is it this time, Siony?!

282
00:09:26,566 --> 00:09:28,734
It's not gossip, Audrey!

283
00:09:28,818 --> 00:09:31,112
It's true! Here's the proof!

284
00:09:31,195 --> 00:09:32,738
[wailing]

285
00:09:34,031 --> 00:09:35,783
Look at this!

286
00:09:37,326 --> 00:09:38,411
Oh, my God!

287
00:09:38,494 --> 00:09:39,203
My God, Lord!

288
00:09:39,287 --> 00:09:41,122
Velma, blur that!

289
00:09:41,205 --> 00:09:44,000
You fool! How can I blur myself?!

290
00:09:44,625 --> 00:09:45,626
[bawls]

291
00:09:45,710 --> 00:09:48,838
Ah, Siony, Siony, take her to
the medic tent first, okay.

292
00:09:48,921 --> 00:09:51,132
Ah, where is Atoy, anyway?!

293
00:09:51,215 --> 00:09:53,551
Well, I didn't notice him there.

294
00:09:53,634 --> 00:09:56,012
[suspicious music playing]

295
00:09:56,095 --> 00:09:57,930
Oh, Audrey? Where are you going?

296
00:09:58,014 --> 00:09:59,432
I'll find Atoy.

297
00:09:59,515 --> 00:10:01,559
Um, tell the remaining runners

298
00:10:01,642 --> 00:10:03,477
and everyone else that they
need to go home.

299
00:10:03,561 --> 00:10:04,562
It's not safe here anymore.

300
00:10:04,645 --> 00:10:05,563
Mmm, no. I'm coming with you.

301
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:07,315
Let's go!

302
00:10:08,649 --> 00:10:09,525
[music fades]

303
00:10:10,234 --> 00:10:11,277
Hey, wait.

304
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:13,654
Well, the zombie might bite me here.

305
00:10:13,738 --> 00:10:14,947
[rousing music playing]

306
00:10:15,031 --> 00:10:17,074
The van is in the garage
now, it's safe.

307
00:10:18,034 --> 00:10:19,327
But you were late.

308
00:10:19,994 --> 00:10:23,039
Because some people attacked us.

309
00:10:23,122 --> 00:10:23,956
What?

310
00:10:25,166 --> 00:10:26,917
They were good, skilled.

311
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:29,086
Driver: And they want to see the big boss.

312
00:10:29,712 --> 00:10:31,756
But you were able to get away?

313
00:10:31,839 --> 00:10:33,549
They’re good, but I'm the best.

314
00:10:33,633 --> 00:10:34,467
[smirks]

315
00:10:36,010 --> 00:10:37,178
Good.

316
00:10:37,261 --> 00:10:39,055
You will receive bonus for this

317
00:10:39,138 --> 00:10:40,097
in your account.

318
00:10:40,181 --> 00:10:41,307
Thank you, Sir.

319
00:10:42,516 --> 00:10:44,435
[rousing music playing]

320
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:48,397
Sir, we have a problem.

321
00:10:50,775 --> 00:10:52,234
Baker escaped.

322
00:10:53,235 --> 00:10:54,153
What are you talking about?

323
00:10:54,236 --> 00:10:55,279
The Baker is dead.

324
00:10:55,363 --> 00:10:56,197
No, Sir.

325
00:10:56,822 --> 00:10:59,450
He escaped while being transported.

326
00:11:00,242 --> 00:11:01,160
He's alive.

327
00:11:01,744 --> 00:11:05,122
Alert all units to look
out for Baker, now!

328
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:07,458
Now!

329
00:11:07,541 --> 00:11:10,836
[rousing music playing]

330
00:11:11,879 --> 00:11:13,464
Bring the ambulance closer.

331
00:11:14,090 --> 00:11:15,633
Wait, I'll come to you.

332
00:11:18,344 --> 00:11:21,222
[pensive music playing]

333
00:11:22,932 --> 00:11:23,766
Baker…

334
00:11:26,394 --> 00:11:27,228
Baker.

335
00:11:28,521 --> 00:11:31,148
Baker, what happened to you?

336
00:11:31,232 --> 00:11:33,567
[music continues]

337
00:11:33,651 --> 00:11:34,777
What did they do to you?

338
00:11:36,862 --> 00:11:38,572
Master Cutter…

339
00:11:38,656 --> 00:11:40,116
[music continues]

340
00:11:40,199 --> 00:11:41,534
It's me.

341
00:11:41,617 --> 00:11:42,993
[music continues]

342
00:11:43,077 --> 00:11:43,911
Baker, you're Dickson.

343
00:11:44,954 --> 00:11:48,999
Dickson, what did they do to you?

344
00:11:50,543 --> 00:11:52,128
What did Obsidian do to you?

345
00:11:52,795 --> 00:11:54,004
Is Mercado there?

346
00:11:54,672 --> 00:11:56,215
Where are you?
What's the location?

347
00:11:57,591 --> 00:11:59,009
What did they do to you?

348
00:12:00,761 --> 00:12:02,179
14…

349
00:12:02,263 --> 00:12:04,932
Dickson: 37, 58.

350
00:12:05,850 --> 00:12:09,854
North, 121, 02.

351
00:12:10,563 --> 00:12:11,814
39, East.

352
00:12:11,897 --> 00:12:13,941
East? Baker…

353
00:12:14,024 --> 00:12:15,359
11… Where is this?

354
00:12:16,444 --> 00:12:18,362
14, East.

355
00:12:18,446 --> 00:12:21,615
- 2… 6.
- 2… and 6.

356
00:12:22,992 --> 00:12:23,784
What else?

357
00:12:23,868 --> 00:12:25,202
Washer.

358
00:12:25,286 --> 00:12:26,120
Atoy: Wa--

359
00:12:26,203 --> 00:12:27,830
[rousing music playing]

360
00:12:27,913 --> 00:12:28,706
Washer.

361
00:12:28,789 --> 00:12:29,707
Washer?

362
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:30,666
Wh--what washer?

363
00:12:30,749 --> 00:12:31,542
Washer.

364
00:12:31,625 --> 00:12:32,460
Washer?

365
00:12:33,002 --> 00:12:33,752
Atoy: Is this a code name?

366
00:12:33,836 --> 00:12:35,129
Ah, what's the washer?

367
00:12:35,212 --> 00:12:36,338
What's the washer?!

368
00:12:36,881 --> 00:12:37,840
Washer--

369
00:12:37,923 --> 00:12:39,008
[quivering breath]

370
00:12:40,092 --> 00:12:42,011
Medic. Medic, medic!

371
00:12:42,887 --> 00:12:43,971
Medic! Medic!

372
00:12:44,054 --> 00:12:45,139
He's having a seizure!

373
00:12:50,978 --> 00:12:52,980
[music fades]

374
00:12:53,063 --> 00:12:55,274
Medic: No pulse, no breathing.

375
00:12:55,357 --> 00:12:57,067
Performing chest compressions.

376
00:12:57,151 --> 00:12:59,487
[tense music playing]

377
00:13:04,116 --> 00:13:05,159
Washer.

378
00:13:05,242 --> 00:13:07,620
[music continues]

379
00:13:08,204 --> 00:13:09,538
Are you okay now?

380
00:13:10,164 --> 00:13:12,416
I can take you to the medic tent.

381
00:13:15,044 --> 00:13:19,298
[phone blipping & clicking]

382
00:13:22,384 --> 00:13:23,344
[phone blips]

383
00:13:26,263 --> 00:13:27,181
[phone blips]

384
00:13:41,695 --> 00:13:42,821
[chuckles softly]

385
00:13:43,989 --> 00:13:48,494
[music continues]

386
00:13:51,539 --> 00:13:55,000
[phone ringing]

387
00:13:55,626 --> 00:13:56,460
Hello, Papi?

388
00:13:57,503 --> 00:13:59,171
Oh, you're at the parking now?

389
00:14:01,048 --> 00:14:02,841
I wanted to meet someone, though.

390
00:14:04,927 --> 00:14:06,345
Okay. Okay, I'm going now.

391
00:14:09,181 --> 00:14:10,391
Oh, here.

392
00:14:10,474 --> 00:14:12,101
Let's clean your wound.

393
00:14:12,184 --> 00:14:14,395
[music continues]

394
00:14:15,688 --> 00:14:17,565
You're so sweet, sir.

395
00:14:17,648 --> 00:14:19,149
But I don't have a wound.

396
00:14:20,067 --> 00:14:21,861
Do you want me to scrape myself for you?

397
00:14:22,319 --> 00:14:23,362
Wait, I can do that.

398
00:14:23,445 --> 00:14:24,780
There, there.

399
00:14:24,864 --> 00:14:25,614
[groans]

400
00:14:25,698 --> 00:14:27,116
There, it's scraped.

401
00:14:27,199 --> 00:14:28,909
This is for you, sir.

402
00:14:28,993 --> 00:14:29,618
Ow. It stings, ah!

403
00:14:29,702 --> 00:14:30,786
Sir--

404
00:14:32,872 --> 00:14:33,914
He disappeared?

405
00:14:34,957 --> 00:14:35,624
Ow.

406
00:14:35,708 --> 00:14:37,167
[sneaky music playing]

407
00:14:37,251 --> 00:14:39,712
Where are Audrey and Oka?

408
00:14:39,795 --> 00:14:40,421
[pants]

409
00:14:40,504 --> 00:14:41,797
Where are they?!

410
00:14:41,881 --> 00:14:42,965
Jona: Oh, Ms. Audrey!

411
00:14:43,048 --> 00:14:44,133
Both: Jona!

412
00:14:44,633 --> 00:14:47,303
Ugh, Ms. Audrey, it's okay.

413
00:14:47,386 --> 00:14:49,013
It turns out it wasn't a zombie.

414
00:14:49,096 --> 00:14:51,557
It was just like a madman
who suddenly attacked.

415
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:53,100
Huh? Oh, what--what happened?

416
00:14:53,183 --> 00:14:56,061
Brother Atoy and the police stopped him.

417
00:14:56,145 --> 00:14:56,896
Where is Atoy?

418
00:14:56,979 --> 00:14:58,522
Well, where's the zombie?

419
00:14:59,189 --> 00:15:00,816
Brother Atoy, I don't know.

420
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:03,068
The zombie, they said he's already
in the medic tent.

421
00:15:04,528 --> 00:15:07,865
Ah, well--

422
00:15:13,078 --> 00:15:15,998
[pensive music playing]

423
00:15:23,631 --> 00:15:25,466
Damn!

424
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:27,968
Is that Chanty again?

425
00:15:28,052 --> 00:15:28,761
[chuckles softly]

426
00:15:28,844 --> 00:15:29,762
Well, who else?

427
00:15:30,971 --> 00:15:33,557
When are you really going
to meet her, bro?

428
00:15:33,641 --> 00:15:34,892
Just meet her already.

429
00:15:35,517 --> 00:15:36,518
We already met.

430
00:15:36,602 --> 00:15:37,227
Gavin: Oh?

431
00:15:37,311 --> 00:15:38,562
She was here at the run earlier.

432
00:15:38,646 --> 00:15:40,022
[suspicious music playing]

433
00:15:40,105 --> 00:15:41,315
Good for you, bro!

434
00:15:42,191 --> 00:15:44,735
Wow, finally my friend
found the courage.

435
00:15:44,818 --> 00:15:45,653
Anyway, next time,

436
00:15:46,153 --> 00:15:48,113
let’s go on a double
date with Karla.

437
00:15:49,198 --> 00:15:50,115
So, G?

438
00:15:51,158 --> 00:15:52,117
Gavin: It's your treat, okay.

439
00:15:52,993 --> 00:15:54,036
O--of course.

440
00:15:54,119 --> 00:15:56,205
[music continues]

441
00:15:58,540 --> 00:15:59,708
[music fades]

442
00:16:06,048 --> 00:16:07,341
[sighs]

443
00:16:08,634 --> 00:16:09,510
Well--

444
00:16:11,428 --> 00:16:12,262
Ow, ow.

445
00:16:12,346 --> 00:16:13,681
Oops, sorry.

446
00:16:16,266 --> 00:16:16,850
[sighs]

447
00:16:16,934 --> 00:16:18,936
His stitches didn't open.

448
00:16:19,603 --> 00:16:21,563
They were just pressed too hard earlier.

449
00:16:22,731 --> 00:16:24,608
- That's why it hurts, that's why it hurts.
- Oops, sorry.

450
00:16:24,692 --> 00:16:26,360
That's why it hurts.

451
00:16:26,443 --> 00:16:27,695
Sorry. Okay, just go gently.

452
00:16:27,778 --> 00:16:28,862
Just around it.

453
00:16:30,114 --> 00:16:34,201
I'm sorry, they got away from us.

454
00:16:34,284 --> 00:16:36,370
[mellow music playing]

455
00:16:36,453 --> 00:16:38,122
Uno: It's because I wasn't
able to help you.

456
00:16:38,205 --> 00:16:40,040
[music continues]

457
00:16:40,124 --> 00:16:41,333
But I'm not weak, okay.

458
00:16:42,334 --> 00:16:43,711
I'm just really injured.

459
00:16:45,045 --> 00:16:46,046
I know.

460
00:16:46,130 --> 00:16:48,549
Aren't you the one who
saved me before?

461
00:16:49,550 --> 00:16:51,385
And you kept me safe after that.

462
00:16:52,344 --> 00:16:53,721
So, don't be embarrased.

463
00:16:53,804 --> 00:16:55,139
This is my way of repaying you.

464
00:16:56,974 --> 00:16:58,100
Ah.

465
00:16:59,309 --> 00:17:02,479
So, you're only doing
this out of gratitude.

466
00:17:03,981 --> 00:17:05,941
Should there be another reason?

467
00:17:11,989 --> 00:17:14,408
[music swells]

468
00:17:16,910 --> 00:17:17,828
Ouch!

469
00:17:18,704 --> 00:17:20,789
Sorry!
[chuckles]

470
00:17:20,873 --> 00:17:24,334
I can't see, I didn't mean to.

471
00:17:25,544 --> 00:17:26,420
[Uno sighs]

472
00:17:26,503 --> 00:17:27,755
You meant to.

473
00:17:27,838 --> 00:17:30,591
No, I swear!

474
00:17:30,674 --> 00:17:32,885
[music continues]

475
00:17:32,968 --> 00:17:33,844
It hurts.

476
00:17:34,511 --> 00:17:35,137
[music fades]

477
00:17:35,220 --> 00:17:36,346
Love?

478
00:17:40,059 --> 00:17:41,101
[pensive music playing]

479
00:17:41,185 --> 00:17:42,352
Atoy!

480
00:17:42,978 --> 00:17:44,980
[music continues]

481
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:55,824
[music fades]

482
00:17:55,908 --> 00:17:58,285
[sneaky music playing]

483
00:18:02,039 --> 00:18:03,791
I'll get to know you at last.

484
00:18:04,333 --> 00:18:05,793
[music continues]

485
00:18:05,876 --> 00:18:06,710
Hey!

486
00:18:07,211 --> 00:18:08,629
Come back here!

487
00:18:08,712 --> 00:18:10,297
Miss! Miss, wait a moment!

488
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:11,965
- Ms. Audrey! Ms. Audrey!
- Excuse me, hello!

489
00:18:12,049 --> 00:18:12,841
[squeals & gasps]

490
00:18:12,925 --> 00:18:13,467
Oh, Ms. Audrey!

491
00:18:13,550 --> 00:18:14,968
You startled me, Jona!

492
00:18:15,052 --> 00:18:16,095
Ah, what the heck?!

493
00:18:16,178 --> 00:18:17,554
This is the liquidation of the zombie run!

494
00:18:17,638 --> 00:18:18,514
So it can be audited right away.

495
00:18:18,597 --> 00:18:20,557
Jona: Are you okay? What
happened to you?!

496
00:18:20,641 --> 00:18:21,391
Where is she?

497
00:18:21,475 --> 00:18:22,684
Huh? Who is she?

498
00:18:23,435 --> 00:18:24,686
Ah, there's--there's a woman.

499
00:18:24,770 --> 00:18:25,854
She--she has a hair clip.

500
00:18:26,396 --> 00:18:28,357
Ah, the same as the hair clip I found

501
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:29,650
inside Atoy's car.

502
00:18:29,733 --> 00:18:30,400
Oh, really?

503
00:18:30,484 --> 00:18:31,527
Well, I followed her but…

504
00:18:31,610 --> 00:18:32,486
she disappeared.

505
00:18:32,569 --> 00:18:33,654
Where is she? Let's follow her!

506
00:18:33,737 --> 00:18:34,279
Let's find her!

507
00:18:35,155 --> 00:18:36,490
because you blocked me!

508
00:18:36,573 --> 00:18:37,991
Jona: Oh, sorry.

509
00:18:38,075 --> 00:18:38,909
I’m sorry.

510
00:18:39,493 --> 00:18:41,829
It's okay, we'll meet again,

511
00:18:42,412 --> 00:18:45,624
and whoever that woman is who's
flirting with my husband,

512
00:18:45,707 --> 00:18:46,875
she'd better get ready.

513
00:18:46,959 --> 00:18:47,459
Jona: Oh.

514
00:18:47,543 --> 00:18:49,294
Because I'll confront her.

515
00:18:49,378 --> 00:18:50,212
Jona: Yes!

516
00:18:51,171 --> 00:18:52,131
Let's confront her.

517
00:18:53,340 --> 00:18:54,299
Oh, well--

518
00:18:54,383 --> 00:18:56,635
Sorry, maybe she's still around.

519
00:18:59,138 --> 00:19:00,264
Ibyang: Wait.

520
00:19:00,764 --> 00:19:02,015
Is it true?

521
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:05,269
You fought a zombie?!

522
00:19:06,395 --> 00:19:07,437
Hmm?

523
00:19:07,521 --> 00:19:09,731
Tell us the story, Tatoy!

524
00:19:09,815 --> 00:19:12,276
Daddy, did you get bitten, Daddy?

525
00:19:12,359 --> 00:19:14,945
Were there other zombies?

526
00:19:15,028 --> 00:19:17,030
Like in, the--what is that?

527
00:19:17,114 --> 00:19:18,240
In the TV show, the one in the movies.

528
00:19:18,323 --> 00:19:20,492
- Atoy: Ah, kids…
- Daddy, you might be infected.

529
00:19:21,535 --> 00:19:22,327
Go to sleep.

530
00:19:22,411 --> 00:19:24,413
We'll tell you the story tomorrow, okay.

531
00:19:24,496 --> 00:19:26,331
Go on, it's late.
Go with your mommy.

532
00:19:26,415 --> 00:19:28,208
Um, love, please make me some tea.

533
00:19:28,292 --> 00:19:29,042
Please?

534
00:19:29,126 --> 00:19:30,002
Come on.

535
00:19:30,085 --> 00:19:31,753
Good night, Tatoy.

536
00:19:31,837 --> 00:19:33,088
Bye, Daddy.

537
00:19:33,172 --> 00:19:34,882
Good night.

538
00:19:34,965 --> 00:19:36,133
Good night.

539
00:19:36,216 --> 00:19:37,176
I'll come back later.

540
00:19:38,343 --> 00:19:40,095
Audrey: Come on, girls! Bedtime.

541
00:19:41,555 --> 00:19:42,890
Janine: Bedtime.

542
00:19:43,682 --> 00:19:47,561
[pensive music playing]

543
00:19:49,271 --> 00:19:52,941
[phone vibrating]

544
00:19:55,485 --> 00:19:56,069
[music fades]

545
00:19:56,153 --> 00:19:56,987
Hello, Uno?

546
00:19:58,030 --> 00:19:59,489
Have you made it back safely?

547
00:20:00,741 --> 00:20:02,576
Belladonna and I are here.

548
00:20:02,659 --> 00:20:04,745
Jesabel also texted me,

549
00:20:04,828 --> 00:20:06,413
she says she's almost here too.

550
00:20:06,496 --> 00:20:09,208
[suspicious music playing]

551
00:20:09,291 --> 00:20:10,667
There's something you need to know.

552
00:20:11,543 --> 00:20:12,794
Dickson Tonido.

553
00:20:14,338 --> 00:20:15,631
That's the name of the…

554
00:20:15,714 --> 00:20:17,216
zombie who attacked me.

555
00:20:18,258 --> 00:20:19,092
He's The Baker.

556
00:20:19,885 --> 00:20:20,928
Sir?

557
00:20:22,095 --> 00:20:23,263
But--

558
00:20:23,347 --> 00:20:24,348
Why, Sir?

559
00:20:24,431 --> 00:20:25,515
Atoy on the phone: I don't know either.

560
00:20:26,141 --> 00:20:27,184
But it seems like…

561
00:20:27,935 --> 00:20:31,104
Obsidian did something to him.

562
00:20:31,188 --> 00:20:33,232
It looks like he was experimented on.

563
00:20:33,315 --> 00:20:34,566
[tense music playing]

564
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:35,817
But where is he, Sir?

565
00:20:36,818 --> 00:20:37,903
Maybe…

566
00:20:38,487 --> 00:20:40,656
Maybe we can talk to him, Sir.

567
00:20:41,573 --> 00:20:42,783
Atoy on the phone: No, he's dead.

568
00:20:43,325 --> 00:20:45,202
[music continues]

569
00:20:45,285 --> 00:20:46,828
I'll go there tomorrow morning.

570
00:20:47,329 --> 00:20:48,455
I'll brief you.

571
00:20:49,665 --> 00:20:50,499
Okay, Sir.

572
00:20:52,459 --> 00:20:54,169
[music fades]

573
00:20:55,712 --> 00:20:57,214
Did you know The Baker?

574
00:20:57,965 --> 00:21:00,425
[somber music playing]

575
00:21:01,218 --> 00:21:02,010
Yeah.

576
00:21:02,094 --> 00:21:03,595
[music continues]

577
00:21:03,679 --> 00:21:05,222
I was partnered with him many times

578
00:21:05,305 --> 00:21:06,890
when I was new at the agency.

579
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:10,018
I also learned a lot from him.

580
00:21:10,978 --> 00:21:14,690
[music continues]

581
00:21:20,821 --> 00:21:22,614
I'm sorry.

582
00:21:22,698 --> 00:21:24,449
[music continues]

583
00:21:27,786 --> 00:21:29,204
Sorry.

584
00:21:30,247 --> 00:21:31,123
[rousing music playing]

585
00:21:31,206 --> 00:21:32,958
I knew it!

586
00:21:33,625 --> 00:21:35,043
Are you flirting with each other?!

587
00:21:35,669 --> 00:21:37,796
Can you not? Read the room!

588
00:21:37,879 --> 00:21:39,548
Nobody is flirting here!

589
00:21:39,631 --> 00:21:41,508
Uno just received bad news!

590
00:21:42,342 --> 00:21:44,094
Read the room, read the room.

591
00:21:44,177 --> 00:21:46,722
[sneaky music playing]

592
00:21:52,394 --> 00:21:53,687
Fine, sorry.

593
00:21:55,605 --> 00:21:57,816
[music fades]

594
00:22:00,027 --> 00:22:03,613
[footsteps tapping]

595
00:22:03,697 --> 00:22:05,782
Love, thank you for the tea!

596
00:22:09,119 --> 00:22:12,039
[suspicious music playing]

597
00:22:12,122 --> 00:22:13,582
[liquid pouring]

598
00:22:14,166 --> 00:22:15,625
[clatters]

599
00:22:15,709 --> 00:22:18,295
[music continues]

600
00:22:22,007 --> 00:22:23,050
Love?

601
00:22:25,510 --> 00:22:27,721
[music continues]

602
00:22:28,388 --> 00:22:29,639
Atoy?

603
00:22:31,558 --> 00:22:35,312
[music continues]

604
00:22:35,395 --> 00:22:38,774
[music continues]

605
00:22:58,668 --> 00:23:00,045
His birthday.

606
00:23:01,671 --> 00:23:02,923
[music fades]

607
00:23:03,006 --> 00:23:03,673
[phone blips]

608
00:23:03,757 --> 00:23:05,634
[heavy music playing]

609
00:23:05,717 --> 00:23:08,011
Our wedding anniversary.

610
00:23:08,095 --> 00:23:09,638
[music continues]

611
00:23:09,721 --> 00:23:10,347
[phone blips]

612
00:23:10,430 --> 00:23:12,390
[music continues]

613
00:23:15,435 --> 00:23:18,021
Ibyang's birthday.

614
00:23:18,105 --> 00:23:19,564
[tense music playing]

615
00:23:20,065 --> 00:23:21,066
[phone blips]

616
00:23:21,149 --> 00:23:22,400
[music continues]

617
00:23:23,026 --> 00:23:24,820
Janine's birthday.

618
00:23:24,903 --> 00:23:25,737
[phone blips]

619
00:23:26,238 --> 00:23:27,489
[music swells]

620
00:23:34,204 --> 00:23:35,247
[music fades]

621
00:23:35,330 --> 00:23:37,290
[tense music playing]

622
00:23:48,218 --> 00:23:52,097
14, 37, 58, North.

623
00:23:53,098 --> 00:23:55,475
121, 2, 39, East.

624
00:23:56,434 --> 00:23:58,520
Did he say anything else?

625
00:23:58,603 --> 00:23:59,312
Yes.

626
00:23:59,396 --> 00:24:01,815
[suspicious music playing]

627
00:24:06,736 --> 00:24:07,988
Washer.

628
00:24:08,738 --> 00:24:10,615
- Jesabel: Ah, Washer.
- Washer.

629
00:24:11,116 --> 00:24:12,159
Jesabel: Ah!

630
00:24:12,242 --> 00:24:13,994
Maybe that's a code name!

631
00:24:14,661 --> 00:24:16,288
A code name, right?

632
00:24:16,371 --> 00:24:18,039
Code name, Washer.

633
00:24:18,123 --> 00:24:19,624
One who washes, one who cleans.

634
00:24:19,708 --> 00:24:21,710
That means maybe he's the one who

635
00:24:21,793 --> 00:24:24,462
cleans up their mess.

636
00:24:25,380 --> 00:24:28,300
And whatever his connection to Obsidian,

637
00:24:28,383 --> 00:24:29,843
he surely knows a lot,

638
00:24:30,927 --> 00:24:32,971
and this is where we'll find him.

639
00:24:33,054 --> 00:24:35,098
[music continues]

640
00:24:35,724 --> 00:24:36,808
Jesabel: Oh.

641
00:24:37,726 --> 00:24:40,937
I thought those were numbers
I'd bet on in the lotto.

642
00:24:41,521 --> 00:24:43,023
So that's what it was.

643
00:24:43,106 --> 00:24:45,233
Obviously, these are coordinates.

644
00:24:45,317 --> 00:24:46,526
This will point us directly

645
00:24:46,610 --> 00:24:47,777
to the location of the Washer.

646
00:24:48,987 --> 00:24:51,489
Showing off again.
[music swells]

647
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:53,408
Showing off.

648
00:24:54,242 --> 00:24:55,869
What's wrong with being good?

649
00:24:55,952 --> 00:24:57,537
Rather than showing off?

650
00:24:58,163 --> 00:24:59,915
Are you referring to me, huh?

651
00:25:00,790 --> 00:25:01,625
You have to admit,

652
00:25:01,708 --> 00:25:04,252
the reason the van we were
following got away from us

653
00:25:04,336 --> 00:25:06,046
is because you showboated.

654
00:25:06,129 --> 00:25:07,923
Guys relax--ow.

655
00:25:08,006 --> 00:25:09,841
Just relax! What is this?

656
00:25:09,925 --> 00:25:11,134
[chuckles sarcastically]

657
00:25:11,218 --> 00:25:12,761
Girl, don't make me lose my temper.

658
00:25:12,844 --> 00:25:13,929
I'm warning you.

659
00:25:14,721 --> 00:25:19,351
You didn't want to listen when we said
not to tailgate, we told you.

660
00:25:19,434 --> 00:25:23,438
You still did it. So, they noticed,
and it got chaotic.

661
00:25:23,521 --> 00:25:26,316
Wow! Then you should have volunteered

662
00:25:26,399 --> 00:25:27,651
to drive, right?

663
00:25:27,734 --> 00:25:29,694
- Psst, psst. Enough--enough.
- You're such a show-off.

664
00:25:29,778 --> 00:25:30,570
[music fades]

665
00:25:30,654 --> 00:25:31,529
Enough, enough.

666
00:25:31,613 --> 00:25:32,989
Stop fighting!

667
00:25:33,073 --> 00:25:34,783
Atoy: That's over, let's move on.

668
00:25:36,284 --> 00:25:38,370
Our focus is Washer.

669
00:25:38,453 --> 00:25:39,871
Let's focus on this.

670
00:25:40,664 --> 00:25:42,249
[tense music playing]

671
00:25:43,124 --> 00:25:45,710
[music swells]

672
00:25:45,794 --> 00:25:50,048
[electronic blipping]

673
00:25:50,131 --> 00:25:51,299
[music fades]

674
00:25:51,383 --> 00:25:55,470
[intense music playing]

675
00:25:56,054 --> 00:25:58,265
Leighton: Why are you lying, Janine?

676
00:25:58,348 --> 00:25:59,808
You're really not Ibyang's sister.

677
00:25:59,891 --> 00:26:00,767
Who said that?

678
00:26:00,850 --> 00:26:01,685
Ibyang!

679
00:26:02,394 --> 00:26:04,396
I got embarrassed because of you!

680
00:26:04,980 --> 00:26:07,816
Gavin! Oh my gosh! It's you!

681
00:26:07,899 --> 00:26:08,817
Gavin!

682
00:26:08,900 --> 00:26:09,442
Why is it like that?

683
00:26:09,526 --> 00:26:10,694
I'll explain to you later.

684
00:26:10,777 --> 00:26:12,195
Just come with me for now.

685
00:26:12,279 --> 00:26:13,613
I know where…

686
00:26:13,697 --> 00:26:15,949
Elvis and Rochelle hang out.

687
00:26:16,032 --> 00:26:17,784
Paldo: You'll see, later
we'll have evidence.

688
00:26:17,867 --> 00:26:18,785
Gotcha!

689
00:26:18,868 --> 00:26:19,744
[groans]

690
00:26:19,828 --> 00:26:22,747
It feels like we've met somewhere before?

691
00:26:22,831 --> 00:26:23,707
That's good enough,
that's good enough.

692
00:26:23,790 --> 00:26:24,624
Wait. Who is that?

693
00:26:24,708 --> 00:26:26,126
Hey, Atoy?

694
00:26:26,209 --> 00:26:26,876
There, he's gone.

695
00:26:26,960 --> 00:26:28,753
Perfectly safe now.
Okay, okay.

696
00:26:28,837 --> 00:26:29,504
Emerson: There.

697
00:26:29,587 --> 00:26:30,422
Hey.

698
00:26:30,505 --> 00:26:31,506
Sorry, sorry, sorry, sorry.

699
00:26:31,589 --> 00:26:32,882
Please excuse them.

700
00:26:32,966 --> 00:26:34,843
Excuse them? They should
apologize to me.

701
00:26:34,926 --> 00:26:36,344
- Wow, seriously.
- No, it's fine now.

702
00:26:36,428 --> 00:26:37,721
Oh, you. Come on,
come on. Let's go.

703
00:26:37,804 --> 00:26:40,181
Emerson: This guy, sometimes it’s like
he's really trying to ruin things.

704
00:26:40,265 --> 00:26:41,808
You just think that.

705
00:26:41,891 --> 00:26:43,184
["Mamang Sastre" playing]
